    <td valign="top"><font face="Trebuchet MS, Arial, Helvetica"> <span class="Heading">Recruiting</span> 
      <p align="center"><font face="Verdana,Arial" size="2">Dusk Eternal is a 
        a close knit guild, but also one based upon freedom and comradery, rather 
        than harsh rules and stringent guidelines.&nbsp; As a result, our recruiting 
        policy is pretty informal.&nbsp; However, under it all lies the central 
        spirit of the guild, we must all get along and we must all be able to 
        work and contribute as a team.<br>
        <font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><br>
        <font color="#FF0000" size="3">The policy is as follows</font></font></font>
      <p><font face="Verdana,Arial" size="2"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">1) 
        Any member can sponsor a new recruit. A member is allowed to sponsor two 
        new recruits at a time.</font></font>
      </font> 
      <p><font size="2" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">2) A new 
        recruit is given an invite to the guild immediately. They will be granted 
        access to most sections of the message board. The &quot;new recruit&quot; 
        status will last for 1 month from the day the recruit was guilded. During 
        this time the guild will make an evaluation of the new recruit and the 
        recruit will get a feel for how the guild works.</font></p>
      <p><font size="2" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">3) At the 
        end of this trial period the guild will have a vote to determine if the 
        recruit becomes a member. Members are not required to vote, however, all 
        members have veto power. Any vote against the new recruit means they will 
        not become a member at that time.</font></p>
      <p><font size="2" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">4)If a new 
        recruit does not receive 100% favorable votes they can opt to stay as 
        a new recruit for one more month. At the end of that month another vote 
        will be taken. If at the end of this month they do not receive 100% favorable 
        votes they will be removed from the guild.</font></p>
      <p><font size="2" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">5)New recruits 
        may be assigned quests or tasks by members at any time. These quests or 
        tasks will meet the following criteria<br>
        a) The quest or task will be possible to complete for someone of the new 
        recruits level, although it may be hard and require cooperation from others.<br>
        b) The quest or task will not be profitable to the guild member assigning 
        it. If the quest is to obtain something of value, they either get to keep 
        the item or something of greater value will be given to the new recruit 
        on completion of the quest or task.<br>
        d) Dusket's resources can be used as rewards for these quests and tasks.</font></p>
      <p><font size="2" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">6) The guild 
        will hold monthly events. During these events new recruits will be granted 
        full guild status should they have received favorable votes.<br>
        </font></p>
      <font face="Trebuchet MS, Arial, Helvetica">
      <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2"><br>
        </font> 
      </font> 
